  "note": "Known headless\u2194desktop parity gaps, recorded when the gate landed. This list may only shrink: `pnpm audit:host-parity` reports (and, once ENFORCE_RATCHET flips, fails on) any new one. Keys are `A:<path>` seam bypass, `B:<section>` desktop-only UI, `C:<command>:<side>` one-sided RPC arm, `E:<feature>:<kind>` capability misreport. Regenerate with `pnpm audit:host-parity:baseline` after paying debt down. The five `A:lib/{ai/agent/team,identity,native,network,server-ops}` rows were not hidden debt anyone chose: the gate stops at its stale-annotation check before it reaches the findings diff, and fifteen annotations had rotted, so these were invisible while it failed for a bookkeeping reason instead. Clearing the rot exposed them. They are recorded rather than fixed because they belong to five different subsystems, and the ratchet still shrank: 201 to 195, with eight closed by the host-neutral keyring and code-server arms. The 2026-11-01 rewrite to 94 also erased nine real gaps (the eight codex_app_* arms rpc/codex_app.rs refuses headless through codex_app_host(), and lib/automation/audit.ts, a type import plus a dynamic listen); the gate now detects both kinds, and they are back.",
